# ===== nnU-Net data directories =====
# Raw, preprocessed, and results/output data produced or consumed by nnU-Net
# should never be committed - it is large, regenerable, and often
# patient/subject data that shouldn't live in git history.
nnUNetFrame/dataset/nnUNet_raw/
nnUNetFrame/dataset/nnUNet_preprocessed/
nnUNetFrame/dataset/nnUNet_predictions/
nnUNetFrame/dataset/label_192/

# nnU-Net results directory: keep configs/metrics, ignore everything else
# (weights, predictions, logs) via the more specific rules below.
nnUNetFrame/dataset/nnUNet_results/**/validation/
nnUNetFrame/dataset/nnUNet_results.zip

# ===== Model weight / checkpoint files (anywhere in the repo) =====
*.pth
*.pt
*.ckpt
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.onnx
*.pb
*.safetensors
*.weights

# ===== Medical imaging / dataset file formats (anywhere in the repo) =====
*.nii
*.nii.gz
*.nrrd
*.mha
*.mhd
*.dcm
*.npy
*.npz

# ===== Archives (often bundled datasets/results) =====
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.7z
